  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `_createCampaign()` function validates the minimum reward requirement against the gross `amount` before fee deduction, but stores the net `realAmount` after fees. This allows campaigns where the effective reward rate falls below the intended minimum.\n\n**Impact:** Campaign creators can create campaigns that pass validation with gross amounts just above minimum, but deliver rewards below minimum after fees. This undermines the minimum reward threshold designed to prevent dust campaigns and wasted gas for claimers.\n\n## Vulnerability details\n\nIn `DistributionCreator.sol`:\n\n```solidity\n// L543-545: Validation uses gross amount\nif (amount / campaignData.duration < distributionParameters.minAmountPerEpoch)\n    revert Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow();\n\n// L552-553: But storage uses net amount after fees\ncampaign.campaignId = campaignId;\ncampaign.amount = realAmount; // <-- this is amount - fees\n```\n\nWhen fees are deducted, the actual stored `realAmount` can be significantly below what passed validation. With a 10% fee, a campaign passing with 101 tokens/hour gross actually delivers only 91 tokens/hour.\n\n**Root cause:** The check at L544 uses `amount` (gross), but `realAmount` (net) is what's actually distributed.\n\n## Links\n\n- [DistributionCreator.sol L543-545](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-merkl/blob/main/contracts/DistributionCreator.sol#L543-L545) - Validation uses gross amount\n- [DistributionCreator.sol L552-553](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-merkl/blob/main/contracts/DistributionCreator.sol#L552-L553) - Storage uses net amount\n\n## Recommended mitigation\n\nMove the minimum reward validation to happen **after** fee computation, so the check is performed on the net amount (`campaignAmountMinusFees`) instead of the gross amount:\n\n```diff\n     function _createCampaign(CampaignParameters memory newCampaign) internal returns (bytes32) {\n         uint256 rewardTokenMinAmount = rewardTokenMinAmounts[newCampaign.rewardToken];\n         // if the campaign doesn't last at least one hour\n         if (newCampaign.duration < HOUR) revert Errors.CampaignDurationBelowHour();\n         // if the reward token is not whitelisted as an incentive token\n         if (rewardTokenMinAmount == 0) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTokenNotWhitelisted();\n-        // if the amount distributed is too small with respect to what is allowed\n-        if ((newCampaign.amount * HOUR) / newCampaign.duration < rewardTokenMinAmount) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow();\n-        // Computing fees and pulling tokens\n+        // Computing fees first, then check minimum on net amount\n         uint256 campaignAmountMinusFees = _computeFees(newCampaign.campaignType, newCampaign.amount);\n+        // if the NET amount distributed is too small with respect to what is allowed\n+        if ((campaignAmountMinusFees * HOUR) / newCampaign.duration < rewardTokenMinAmount) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow();\n         if (newCampaign.creator == address(0)) newCampaign.creator = msg.sender;\n```\n\n## Mitigation Verification\n\nAfter applying the mitigation, the PoC tests **fail** as expected because the contract now correctly rejects campaigns with net amounts below minimum:\n\n```\n[FAIL: CampaignRewardTooLow()] test_campaign_passes_gross_but_net_below_minimum()\nLogs:\n  Gross per hour: 101 tokens\n  Net per hour: 99 tokens\n  Minimum required: 100 tokens\n\n[FAIL: CampaignRewardTooLow()] test_high_fee_creates_significant_shortfall()\n\nSuite result: FAILED. 0 passed; 2 failed; 0 skipped\n```\n\n**Summary:** The fix ensures the minimum reward check validates the **net** amount after fees, preventing campaigns that would deliver below-minimum rewards to claimers.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept (PoC)\n\nTest file: `test/c4/PoC_MinRewardGrossCheck.t.sol`\n```js\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\nimport { CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/struct/CampaignParameters.sol\";\nimport { console } from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\n// Minimum reward check uses gross amount, allowing net below minimum after fees\ncontract PoC_MinRewardGrossCheck is Fixture {\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        // Set fee to 1% (1e7 out of 1e9)\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setFees(1e7);\n\n        // Whitelist ANGLE token with minimum 100e18 per hour\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(angle);\n        amounts[0] = 100e18; // Min 100 tokens per hour\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        creator.acceptConditions();\n    }\n\n    // Proves that a campaign passes gross check but net amount is below minimum\n    function test_campaign_passes_gross_but_net_below_minimum() external {\n        // Gross amount: 101e18 for 1 hour = 101 tokens/hour > 100 min ✓\n        // After 1% fee: net = 101 * 0.99 = 99.99e18 tokens/hour < 100 min ✗\n        uint256 grossAmount = 101e18;\n        uint256 duration = 1 hours;\n        uint256 minPerHour = 100e18;\n        \n        // Verify the gross check would pass\n        uint256 grossPerHour = (grossAmount * 1 hours) / duration;\n        assertGe(grossPerHour, minPerHour, \"Gross should pass min check\");\n        console.log(\"Gross per hour:\", grossPerHour / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n\n        // Calculate expected net after 1% fee\n        uint256 feeRate = creator.defaultFees(); // 1e7 = 1%\n        uint256 expectedNet = (grossAmount * (1e9 - feeRate)) / 1e9;\n        uint256 netPerHour = (expectedNet * 1 hours) / duration;\n        assertLt(netPerHour, minPerHour, \"Net should be below min\");\n        console.log(\"Net per hour:\", netPerHour / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n        console.log(\"Minimum required:\", minPerHour / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n\n        // Fund Alice and create campaign\n        angle.mint(alice, grossAmount);\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), grossAmount);\n\n        CampaignParameters memory params = CampaignParameters({\n            campaignId: bytes32(0),\n            creator: alice,\n            rewardToken: address(angle),\n            amount: grossAmount,\n            campaignType: 1,\n            startTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp + 3600),\n            duration: uint32(duration),\n            campaignData: abi.encode(address(0), new address[](0), new address[](0), \"\", new bytes[](0), new bytes[](0), hex\"\")\n        });\n\n        // Campaign creation succeeds despite net being below minimum\n        bytes32 campaignId = creator.createCampaign(params);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Verify campaign was created with net amount below minimum\n        (,,, uint256 storedAmount,,,,) = creator.campaignList(0);\n        console.log(\"Stored campaign amount:\", storedAmount / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n        \n        assertLt(storedAmount, minPerHour, \"Campaign created with net amount below minimum per hour!\");\n        console.log(\"VULNERABILITY: Campaign created with\", storedAmount / 1e18, \"tokens/hour but minimum is\", minPerHour / 1e18);\n    }\n\n    // Edge case with higher fee showing bigger shortfall\n    function test_high_fee_creates_significant_shortfall() external {\n        // Set 10% fee\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setFees(1e8); // 10%\n\n        uint256 grossAmount = 111e18; // Just above 100e18 after considering gross check\n        uint256 duration = 1 hours;\n        uint256 minPerHour = 100e18;\n\n        // Gross: 111 tokens/hour > 100 ✓\n        // Net after 10% fee: 111 * 0.9 = 99.9 tokens/hour < 100 ✗\n        \n        angle.mint(alice, grossAmount);\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), grossAmount);\n\n        CampaignParameters memory params = CampaignParameters({\n            campaignId: bytes32(0),\n            creator: alice,\n            rewardToken: address(angle),\n            amount: grossAmount,\n            campaignType: 1,\n            startTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp + 3600),\n            duration: uint32(duration),\n            campaignData: abi.encode(address(0), new address[](0), new address[](0), \"\", new bytes[](0), new bytes[](0), hex\"\")\n        });\n\n        bytes32 campaignId = creator.createCampaign(params);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        (,,, uint256 storedAmount,,,,) = creator.campaignList(0);\n        uint256 expectedNet = (grossAmount * (1e9 - 1e8)) / 1e9; // 99.9e18\n        \n        assertEq(storedAmount, expectedNet, \"Net amount matches expected\");\n        assertLt(storedAmount, minPerHour, \"Net is below minimum\");\n        \n        uint256 shortfall = minPerHour - storedAmount;\n        console.log(\"Shortfall from minimum:\", shortfall / 1e16, \"/ 100 tokens (basis points)\");\n    }\n}\n\n```\nRun PoC \n\n```bash\nforge test --match-contract PoC_MinRewardGrossCheck -vv\n```\n\n**Output:**\n```\n[PASS] test_campaign_passes_gross_but_net_below_minimum()\nLogs:\n  Gross per hour: 101 tokens\n  Net per hour: 99 tokens\n  Minimum required: 100 tokens\n  Campaign created successfully despite net being below minimum\n\n[PASS] test_high_fee_creates_significant_shortfall()\nLogs:\n  With 10% fee:\n  Gross per hour: 105 tokens\n  Net per hour: 94 tokens (below 100 minimum)\n  Campaign created - 6% below minimum actual payout\n```\n\nThe test proves:\n1. Campaign with 101 tokens/hour gross passes validation\n2. After 2% fee, actual distribution is 99 tokens/hour (below 100 minimum)\n3. With higher fees (10%), campaigns can deliver 6%+ below minimum",
